// run and a suffix run and validated NEITHER domain, so `0b2` `0b12` `0o8` `0o9` `0x` `0b` `0o` `1e` `1i7` `1u7`
// `1x` `1.0f16` all compiled clean. TWELVE measured over-acceptances, ONE shape: the run is consumed, nothing
// checks it. The refusal machinery was already at this site (C-S1-LIT-OVERFLOW-REFUSE), so this is routing, not
// a missing mechanism -- classified by probe before costing, per docs/pin-art-probing.md.
// Sweep also confirmed the ACCEPT side is untouched: 0b101, 0o17, 0xFF, 0x_1, 0x__1, 1__0, 1e5, 1e-5, 1i32,
// 1usize, 1f64, 1.0f32 all still agree with rustc.
