// C-S9-USER-ITER-COLLECT: `<it>.collect::<Vec<_>>()` where `it` is a USER Iterator (a struct with a `next()`
// -> Option method), as opposed to the adaptor chains s9_chain_go handles. Loop: call it.next() (mutates the
// iterator in place through its self pointer), break on the None tag (0), push the Some payload (@8) into a
// fresh Vec. rustc_parse_format's `Parser::new(..).collect::<Vec<Piece>>()` is exactly this.
// A user Iterator (impl Iterator for T) driven through an ADAPTER chain: `c.filter(p).map(f).sum()`. The
// materialize mechanism already exists (s9_user_iter_collect_call loops next() into a Vec) and the vec-adapter
// loop already exists (s9_chain_loop_hdr_b); this wires them -- detect a user-iterator base under 1-or-2 map/filter
// adapters, materialize it, run the hdr_b chain (ak0 inner applied first, ak outer). -1 if not this shape.
