// against an undefined symbol and SEGV. For a generic param the only `From` reachable at that erased position is
// value-identity (char::from(char), char::from(u8), i64::from(i32) are all value-preserving), so emit the argument
// directly. Discriminated by the Rust generic-param naming convention: the type seg is a short all-uppercase name
// (T, U, K, V, ...), which is never a registered concrete type whose real From we would want to call.
// (rustc_lexer scan_escape's `Ok(T::from(res))` is exactly this.)
