// IO-SINK (graphviz / io::Write arc): unified io::Write sink append. The sink is a FILE/STDOUT handle
// ({marker@0, fd@4}) -> syscall write(fd); else a Vec<u8> byte-buffer (SLOTTED, the normal Vec<u8> layout
// that String::from_utf8/fs::write expect) -> push each byte of the PACKED source as an 8-byte slot via
// __vec_push. This replaces the old __scat_s (packed) append for io::Write sinks, which corrupted a Vec<u8>
// buffer read back by from_utf8. fmt::Write (write! to a String) keeps __scat_s. Gated on S9_USESIO.
